      "description": "Watch Elche vs Real Madrid highlights and goals from La Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 15, 2026. On September 15, 2026, La Liga delivered a captivating encounter between Elche and Real Madrid . What began as a controlled performance by the visitors transformed into a high-octane thriller that kept supporters guessing until the final seconds. Early Fortunes for the Visitors Real Madrid opened the match with clinical intent, finding themselves ahead in the 25th minute through a stroke of luck. An unfortunate own goal by Elche goalkeeper Matias Dituro broke the deadlock, giving the giants from the capital an early platform to build upon. Despite Elche ’s efforts to maintain possession, the visitors looked the more dangerous side in the opening exchanges. The lead was doubled in the 33rd minute following a swift attacking move. Federico Valverde released Yan Diomande , who provided the final pass for Kylian Mbappé . The French superstar made no mistake, finishing clinically with his right foot to put Real Madrid in what appeared to be a commanding position before the half-time whistle. Elche’s Spirited Second-Half Fightback The dynamic of the game shifted significantly after the break. Elche refused to concede defeat and began to dominate proceedings, eventually ending the match with 56% possession. Their persistence paid off in the 71st minute when Lucas Cepeda set up Abiel Osorio for a powerful header that flew into the back of the net, breathing new life into the contest. The momentum remained firmly with the hosts as the minutes ticked away. In the 83rd minute, the comeback was complete. Substitute Josan turned provider for Fer Nino , who struck a precise right-footed shot past the goalkeeper to level the scores at 2-2. The stadium erupted as Elche looked set to secure at least a point against the reigning heavyweights. Late Substitute Drama With the clock winding down, Real Madrid coach turned to his bench, introducing Carlos Espi in the 87th minute. The tactical move proved to be a masterstroke. In the first minute of stoppage time, Jude Bellingham orchestrated a move that saw Kylian Mbappé lay the ball off for Carlos Espi . The young striker tapped it home with ease to restore the lead for the visitors. The closing stages were marred by rising tensions, as the referee issued yellow cards to Josan and Gonzalo Villar for unsportsmanlike conduct during a heated scuffle. Though Real Madrid were pushed to their limits, the late intervention from Espi ensured they left with all three points on a night of extraordinary drama."
